# Force source files to always be treated as text, so a stray control byte
# (e.g. a raw NUL in a string literal) can never make a source file render as
# "Binary files differ" and thus slip through code review unseen. See the
# trust-envelope.ts incident fixed in the same series as this file's addition.
#
# `text` normalizes line endings in the index; `eol=lf` also keeps Windows
# checkouts compatible with the repo's formatters. `diff` overrides git's
# NUL-byte binary heuristic so these paths always produce a textual diff.
*.ts    text eol=lf diff
*.tsx   text eol=lf diff
*.js    text eol=lf diff
*.mjs   text eol=lf diff
*.cjs   text eol=lf diff
*.jsx   text eol=lf diff
*.rs    text eol=lf diff
*.py    text eol=lf diff
*.sh    text eol=lf diff
*.json  text eol=lf diff
*.jsonc text eol=lf diff
*.toml  text eol=lf diff
*.yaml  text eol=lf diff
*.yml   text eol=lf diff
*.css   text eol=lf diff
*.scss  text eol=lf diff
*.html  text eol=lf diff
*.md    text eol=lf diff
*.sql   text eol=lf diff
